cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss PhO Token Wire, please cite Christian Heinrich Hohlfeld."
title: "PhO Token Wire: Client-Side Semantic Token Reduction and Local Response Rehydration for LLM Web Chats"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Hohlfeld"
    given-names: "Christian Heinrich"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6634-9045"
website: "https://christianhohlfeld.com/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChristianHohlfeld/PhO-Token-Wire"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-13"
abstract: >-
  Chrome Manifest V3 research prototype for reducing LLM web-chat transport text
  through conservative client-side prompt redundancy reduction, tokenizer-cost
  gating, a compact semantic K/F/U/N response wire format, and local browser
  rehydration of presentation structure.
keywords:
  - LLM
  - token compression
  - semantic compression
  - browser extension
  - PhO-Compress
